{"name":"Twill","hex":"#a3957c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"twill","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A pattern, characterised by diagonal ridges, created by the regular interlacing of threads of the warp and weft during weaving.","A cloth or portion of cloth woven in such a pattern."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To weave (cloth, etc.) so as to produce the appearance of diagonal lines or ribs on the surface."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/twill"}],"entries":[{"title":"Twill","blocks":[{"text":"Twill is a type of textile weave with a pattern of parallel, diagonal ribs. It is one of three fundamental types of weave, along with plain weave and satin. It is made by passing the weft thread over one or more warp threads then under two or more warp threads and so on, with a \"step\", or offset, between rows to create the characteristic diagonal pattern. Due to this structure, twill generally drapes well."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/29/TwillSample.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twill"},{"title":"Twill (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Twill  is a Japanese duo composed of twins Michiko and Yoko. Their stage name is a portmanteau of English language words \"twin\" and \"will\". They are managed by TV Asahi Music."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/Twill_3.jpg/330px-Twill_3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Twill_(band)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Twill_structure.png/250px-Twill_structure.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d0/Twill_structure.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/Twill_structure.png/250px-Twill_structure.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 3/1 twill, as used in denim","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATwill_structure.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d0/22twillsm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/d/d0/22twillsm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Structure of a .mw-parser-output .frac{white-space:nowrap}.mw-parser-output .frac .num,.mw-parser-output .frac .den{font-size:80%;line-height:0;vertical-align:super}.mw-parser-output .frac .den{vertical-align:sub}.mw-parser-output .sr-only{border:0;clip:rect(0,0,0,0);clip-path:polygon(0px 0px,0px 0px,0px 0px);height:1px;margin:-1px;overflow:hidden;padding:0;position:absolute;width:1px}2⁄2 twill. The offset at each row forms the diagonal pattern.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A22twillsm.png"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/06/31twillsm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/06/31twillsm.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Structure of a 3⁄1 twill","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A31twillsm.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/K%C3%B6perbindung_Fischgrat.jpeg/250px-K%C3%B6perbindung_Fischgrat.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/K%C3%B6perbindung_Fischgrat.jpeg/500px-K%C3%B6perbindung_Fischgrat.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/K%C3%B6perbindung_Fi